  id: W6_C
  era: Launched 19 April 1975
  title: Aryabhata, India's first satellite (replica)
  text: Aryabhata, India's first satellite (replica). Named after the 5th-century mathematician and astronomer, India's first satellite was designed and built by ISRO in Bengaluru and launched by a Soviet rocket on 19 April 1975. Its faces were covered with solar cells. It carried experiments in X-ray astronomy and solar physics. Aryabhata began a journey that led to India's own launch rockets, the Chandrayaan missions to the Moon and the Mangalyaan mission to Mars.
